// SPEC 10.5.1, 10.1, 10.4 step 1, 10.6 (PLAN G924 AF-3b; design-af3 Revision 2 and its coverage table, the labels written from SPEC
// before any run): a nested call, construction or contextual Case that awaits its call is checked against the expected Type at its
// position under each remaining candidate, once per distinct Type. A candidate at whose Type it does not check (its own resolution there
// has no applicable candidate or is ambiguous) is inapplicable, its record naming the part, the Type and that outcome; any other outcome
// keeps it, ranked by the class the resolution gives (a borrowed temporary of an owner value at `ref/U`, a value read of a borrow value
// by value, else Expected-Type fitting). Each row is the coverage row of its name; a `-r` row declares the overloads in the opposite
// order. A resolution past IMPL A.4's 4,096 queries is a Resource error (tv11, tv12; the owner's O-351 (a)).
public partial class ApplicabilityChainRegressionTest
